# QA workspace settings (identifiers and settings only, never secrets). Copy to claude.env if you need it.
# AISDLC_ROOT is resolved from the current folder automatically; set it only to run from elsewhere.
#
# Credentials never go in this file (Claude can read it):
#   QA_USERNAME, QA_PASSWORD   test account for the target environment (login.mode "form"): environment variables,
#                              or .env in this folder (gitignored; Claude is denied access to it)
#   JIRA_EMAIL, JIRA_API_TOKEN Jira (reads through the MCP adapter; defect/results comments and uploads):
#                              environment variables only (the Jira MCP server reads them from the environment)
# PowerShell, same session before starting Claude Code:  $env:QA_USERNAME = "qa.bot@example.com"
# or set them once as user environment variables. Check with: node <plugin>/scripts/qa/cred-check.js

# Default target environment (a key of config/environments.yaml). Never production.
# QA_ENV=qa

# Watch-mode slow motion per browser action, in milliseconds (plugin default 500).
# QA_SLOWMO=500
